            <ArticleTitle>Manipulation for the treatment of occupational low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-97</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Manual medicine techniques are performed to correct abnormal structural findings of tenderness, asymmetry, restricted range of motion, and tissue texture changes. Nonthrusting methods include articulatory, muscle energy, functional, counter-strain, and soft tissue manipulations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
